Figure 1.
Cell membrane-coated uricase-loaded MOF nanoparticles for the enzymatic degradation of uric acid. To fabricate the formulation, MOF-uricase cores are generated by mixing the enzyme payload with \(\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}\) and 2-methylimidazole (mim), followed by coating with natural cell membrane derived from source cells such as RBCs or MΦs. The resulting membrane-coated MOF-uricase nanoparticles effectively convert uric acid into allantoin, which can help to manage conditions such hyperuricemia and gout.
